course: dictionary
lesson: 16156
title: Withered: dried up and shrunk
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture for you. «The withered flowers hung over the edge of the vase.» Flowers that hang down, look brown and papery, and have no water left must be dried up. Withered means dried up and shrunk.
explain: Withered is the past form of the verb wither, so you will also see «The leaves withered in the autumn wind» and «The plant withers without water.» The verb tells you what is happening: something is slowly drying up and getting smaller.
explain: Withered can also describe people. «Grandad's withered hand was thin and wrinkled, so he held his cup with care.» The clues are thin and wrinkled, so withered means weak and shrunk with age, not wet or bright. Always check which meaning fits the words around it.
fact: Withered means dried up and shrunk, like an old plant or flower.
fact: Withered can also describe old, wrinkled skin or weak limbs.
fact: Withered is the past form of the verb wither: wither, withers, withered, withering.
fact: Plants wither when they do not get enough water.
fact: In the Bible, Jesus heals a man with a withered hand.
exercise: «The withered flowers hung over the edge of the vase.» What does withered mean? | Bright and full of colour | *Dried up and shrunk | Freshly picked and wet | Very tall and strong
exercise: Why do plants wither? | They are painted with bright colours | They get too much sun to ever grow | *They do not get enough water | They are happy and full of song
exercise: «The leaves withered in the autumn wind.» Which word is the past form of the verb wither? | wind | autumn | *withered | leaves
test: «The rose bush withered after weeks with no rain.» What does withered mean here? | *Dried up and shrunk | Painted bright red | Growing very fast | Covered in fresh dew
test: Which word could describe old, wrinkled skin? | Soaked | Giant | Glowing | *Withered
exam: Which sentence shows a plant that is dried up? | The puppy was withered and happy | The fresh daisies were withered and bright | The sky was withered and blue | *The flowers in the vase were withered and brown
